{% doc %}
  blocks/_article-image.liquid — private.

  The article's picture, and the pills that sit on it.

  ## The frame is this block's, the picture is `snippets/image.liquid`'s

  Ratio, srcset, mobile art direction and the fade-in on load all come from the
  shared snippet, so this file adds only what a card needs on top: a border, a
  radius, and the meta that belongs *on* the photograph rather than under it.

  Ratio is the theme's usual seven names through `snippets/aspect-ratio.liquid`,
  which is why **Landscape** here means the same shape it means on an Image
  block and on a product card.

  ## The date and the tags are pills on the image, not a line of meta

  In the design they sit along the bottom edge of the picture, over a frosted
  panel, which is why they are here and not in **Article content**: they are
  positioned against the photograph and would have nothing to sit on anywhere
  else. Both are off-switchable because a store whose articles are untagged
  should not get an empty row of nothing.

  Two tags at most, and that is deliberate rather than configurable. The pills
  run along one edge of a card that is a third of a row wide; a fifth tag does
  not wrap onto a second line, it pushes the first four off the picture.

  The tags share a wrapper so a phone can put them on their own line under the
  date. It is `display: contents` above 750px, so the desktop row is the same
  single line of pills it was before the wrapper existed.

  ## The image is a link, and it is hidden from assistive technology

  `tabindex="-1"` and `aria-hidden` on the wrapper: the title below is already a
  link to the same article, and a second one with no text of its own is a stop
  on the keyboard path that announces nothing. Sighted pointer users still get
  the whole picture as a target, which is what they expect from a card.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign article = closest.article
  assign s = block.settings

  assign ratio = s.ratio | default: 'landscape'
  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 24 | plus: 0

  comment
    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` here
    would fade the photograph along with its frame.

    With no colour picked the border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters
    cannot take an alpha channel from — there is nothing to read until the
    scheme resolves in the browser. `color-mix` does the same fade at that point
    instead, so both paths honour the slider.
  endcomment
  assign border_width = 0
  if s.border_style != 'none' and s.border_style != blank
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign show_date = s.show_date
  assign show_tags = s.show_tags

  assign has_meta = false
  if show_date or show_tags
    assign has_meta = true
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    ---- what the picture does under a pointer ----

    The same four answers `blocks/_feature-card.liquid` gives, resolved the same
    way and named from the same place — `t:shared.image_effect` — so "Zoom in"
    means one thing across the theme and a merchant learns the control once.

    Zoom is a hover effect and Drift is a scroll effect, which is why they are
    one select rather than a pair of toggles: they animate the same `transform`
    on the same element, and two controls able to ask for both would resolve to
    whichever declaration came last in the stylesheet.

    Nothing here needs the picture to be clipped, because it already is:
    `.article-image-block` carries the corner radius and `overflow: hidden` so
    the rounded frame never sits over square corners. A scaled photograph is
    clipped by the same rule, for free.

    Drift is `<parallax-media>`, the element the hero uses, rather than
    `motion-effect data-effect="parallax"`. The two are different mechanisms:
    motion-effect translates the element and needs 120px of overscan around it —
    a number coupled by hand to a clamp in `assets/motion-engine.js` — while
    `<parallax-media>` writes `--parallax-offset` and lets CSS combine it with a
    `scale()`, which covers the travel with no second number to keep in step.

    The speed is converted here, not passed through. The engine wants a
    multiplier and the schema stores a percentage a merchant can reason about;
    handing 30 to a function that clamps at 0.5 pins every card to maximum
    strength and the slider stops doing anything.
    `snippets/background-image.liquid` documents this as the bug it had.
  endcomment
  assign image_effect = s.hover_image_effect | default: 'zoom_in'

  assign image_scale = s.hover_image_scale | default: 106 | plus: 0
  assign image_scale = image_scale | divided_by: 100.0

  assign drift_speed = s.hover_image_parallax_speed | default: 30 | plus: 0
  if drift_speed < 10
    assign drift_speed = 10
  endif
  if drift_speed > 50
    assign drift_speed = 50
  endif
  assign drift_speed = drift_speed | divided_by: 100.0

  assign layer_tag = 'div'
  if image_effect == 'drift'
    assign layer_tag = 'parallax-media'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture image_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --article-image-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --article-image-transition: {{ s.hover_duration | default: 600 | plus: 0 }}ms;
  {%- if image_effect == 'zoom_in' or image_effect == 'zoom_out' -%}
    --article-image-scale: {{ image_scale }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --article-image-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
    --article-image-border-style: {{ s.border_style }};
    --article-image-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if article -%}
  <div
    class="article-image-block"
    data-block-spacing
    style="{{ image_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <a
      class="article-image-block__link"
      href="{{ article.url }}"
      tabindex="-1"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      {%- comment -%}
        One inner layer, whichever effect is on it — a `<div>` for none and the
        two zooms, `<parallax-media>` for Drift. The class is the same either
        way, so the sizing rules in `base.css` do not have to know which element
        they got, and the modifier is the only thing that varies.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <{{ layer_tag }}
        class="article-image-block__layer article-image-block__layer--{{ image_effect | replace: '_', '-' }}"
        {% if image_effect == 'drift' %}data-speed="{{ drift_speed }}"{% endif %}
      >
        {% render 'image',
           image: article.image,
           ratio: ratio,
           mobile_ratio: s.ratio_mobile,
           sizes: sizes,
           priority: priority,
           placeholder: 'blog-apparel-1',
           wrapper_class: 'article-image-block__media' %}
      </{{ layer_tag }}>
    </a>

    {%- if has_meta -%}
      <div class="article-image-block__meta">
        {%- if show_date -%}
          <span class="article-image-block__pill article-image-block__pill--date">
            {%- if s.date_icon != 'none' and s.date_icon != blank -%}
              <span class="article-image-block__pill-icon">
                {% render 'icon', icon: s.date_icon, size: 14 %}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <time datetime="{{ article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">
              {{- article.published_at | date: format: 'date' -}}
            </time>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if show_tags and article.tags.size > 0 -%}
          <span class="article-image-block__meta-tags">
            {%- for tag in article.tags limit: 2 -%}
              <span class="article-image-block__pill article-image-block__pill--tag">{{ tag }}</span>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.article_image.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "ratio",
      "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "square", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "portrait", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "landscape", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "wide", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "tall", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__6.label" },
        { "value": "long", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__7.label" }
      ],
      "default": "landscape"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "ratio_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio_mobile.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio_mobile.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "square", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "portrait", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "landscape", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "tall", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__6.label" },
        { "value": "long", "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.ratio.options__7.label" }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.image_effect.header" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:shared.image_effect.paragraph" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "hover_image_effect",
      "label": "t:shared.image_effect.label",
      "info": "t:shared.image_effect.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.image_effect.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "zoom_in", "label": "t:shared.image_effect.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "zoom_out", "label": "t:shared.image_effect.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "drift", "label": "t:shared.image_effect.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "zoom_in"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_image_scale",
      "label": "t:shared.image_effect.scale.label",
      "info": "t:shared.image_effect.scale.info",
      "min": 100,
      "max": 140,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 106,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.hover_image_effect == 'zoom_in' or block.settings.hover_image_effect == 'zoom_out' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_image_parallax_speed",
      "label": "t:shared.image_effect.speed.label",
      "info": "t:shared.image_effect.speed.info",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 30,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.hover_image_effect == 'drift' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_duration",
      "label": "t:shared.image_effect.duration.label",
      "info": "t:shared.image_effect.duration.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1200,
      "step": 50,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 600,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.hover_image_effect != 'none' and block.settings.hover_image_effect != 'drift' }}"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.borders" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_style.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:shared.options.solid" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:shared.border.style.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
      "label": "t:shared.border.thickness.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:blocks.image.settings.border_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:shared.border.color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_radius.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.article_image.headers.meta" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.article_image.paragraphs.meta" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_date",
      "label": "t:blocks.article_image.settings.show_date.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "date_icon",
      "label": "t:blocks.article_image.settings.date_icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "clock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__8.label" },
        { "value": "note", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__11.label" },
        { "value": "info", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__12.label" },
        { "value": "tag", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "clock",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.show_date }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_tags",
      "label": "t:blocks.article_image.settings.show_tags.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.article_image.settings.show_tags.info",
      "default": true
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_header" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
